# What never goes into the image.
#
# This file is not housekeeping. `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would otherwise carry `data/` into
# the image, and `backend/data/` is where this project keeps the things that must never leave the
# machine: the reset and opening-balances dumps, the spreadsheets, and the nightly backups the job
# writes to `data/backups/`. An image is a file that gets pushed, pulled and kept — exactly the
# wrong place for the register.
data/
secrets/
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Anything which is not source.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
